# Public Constants Contract

`packages/sdk/index.ts` re-exports plain constants alongside RPC methods —
`ModelType`, `MODEL_TYPES`, `PLUGIN_LLM` and friends, `SUPPORTED_AUDIO_FORMATS`,
`VLA_DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIZE`, `TOOLS_MODE`, `VERBOSITY`. Non-JS SDKs (Python, ...)
are generated from `packages/sdk/contract/{schema.json,manifest.json,
models.json,constants.json}` — they never read `index.ts` directly. A
constant that isn't in one of those artifacts is invisible to every other
language, no matter how prominently it's exported from JS.

`schema.json`/`manifest.json` only capture what's expressible as Zod wire
schemas (RPC request/response fields). A hand-authored `export const FOO =
{...}` with no Zod schema behind it — which is what `ModelType`, `PLUGIN_*`,
`SUPPORTED_AUDIO_FORMATS`, and `VLA_DEFAULT_IMAGE_SIZE` all were before this
rule existed — has no path into the contract at all. It won't cause a build
failure; it just silently never reaches Python (or the next language).

## The rule

When you add a new constant to `index.ts` that other-language consumers
should get as a typed, named value (not just baked into a wire schema's
`enum`), you MUST:

1. Express it as a `z.enum(...)` (for a name→value map — works for both
   string and number values, and for a bare array of strings via identity
   mapping) or `z.literal(...)` (for a standalone scalar).
2. Add it to `constantsRegistry` or `scalarConstantsRegistry` in
   `packages/sdk/schemas/constants-registry.ts`.
3. Run `bun run contract:export` and commit the resulting
   `contract/constants.json` diff.

That's the whole obligation — `build-constants-registry.ts` is generic over
the registered schema's shape (reads `.enum` / `.value`), so a new registry
entry needs no exporter code changes, and downstream generators (starting
with `packages/sdk-python`) pick up new entries automatically on their next
regen.

```ts
// schemas/constants-registry.ts
export const constantsRegistry = {
  ModelType: z.enum(ModelType),
  // new: MyNewThing: z.enum(MyNewThing),
} as const
```

Don't register a constant that's already fully described by a wire schema's
own `z.enum`/`z.literal` field type with no separate named-constant object
behind it — that's already in `schema.json` and doesn't need a second,
redundant entry here. This rule is specifically for constants exported as
their own standalone JS value.

See `packages/sdk/contract/README.md` for the exported shape, and
`.cursor/rules/sdk/sdk-pod-packages.mdc` for what counts as an SDK pod
package this applies to.
